u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0013 SEQ CHAPTER \\h \\r 1\u0015MINUTES OF A REGULAR MEETING OF\rTHE CITY COUNCIL OF THE CITY OF CALABASAS,\rCALIFORNIA, HELD WEDNESDAY, FEBRUARY 7, 2007\r\rMayor Washburn called the meeting to order at 6:30 p.m. in Conference Room No. 2, 26135 Mureau Road, Calabasas, California.\r\rROLL CALL Present: Mayor Washburn, Mayor pro Tem Bozajian, Councilmembers Groveman, Maurer, Wolfson.\r Absent: None.\r Staff: Colantuono, Coroalles, Tamuri.\r\rCLOSED SESSION\r\rThe City Council recessed at 6:31 p.m. into closed session to confer with legal counsel regarding the following:\r\rPending litigation, pursuant to Government Code Section 54946.9(a), City of Calabasas v. RCS II Development Company, et al., BC 339068.\r\rPending litigation, pursuant to Government Code Section 54946.9(a), Smith v. City of Calabasas, BS106644.\r\rPersonnel Matter, pursuant to Government Code, Section 54957:\r PUBLIC EMPLOYEE PERFORMANCE EVALUATION, Title: City Manager\r \rConference with Labor Negotiator, pursuant to Government Code 54957.6\rCity Negotiator: Michael G. Colantuono, City Attorney\rUnrepresented Employee: Anthony Coroalles, City Manager\r\rThe City Council reconvened at 7:20 p.m. from closed session and Mayor Washburn called the meeting to order at 7:35 p.m. in the City Council Chambers of City Hall, 26135 Mureau Road, Calabasas, California.\r\rROLL CALL Present: Mayor Washburn, Mayor pro Tem Bozajian, Councilmembers Groveman, Maurer, Wolfson.\r Absent: None.\r Staff: Bartlett, Colantuono, Coroalles, Lysik, Peirce.\r\rThe Pledge of Allegiance was led by Alan Meyer.\r\rMichael G. Colantuono, City Attorney, stated that on Item #1, the Council accepted and offered a settlement to one of the parties; he stated that the Council did not take any action on Item #2 which required reporting. Mayor Washburn reported that the Council performed the City Manager�s evaluation.\r\rAPPROVAL OF AGENDA\r\r The City Council approved the revised agenda with the continuance of Item #2 and Item #12. MOTION CARRIED 5/0. \r\rANNOUNCEMENTS/INTRODUCTIONS\r\rCity Manager Coroalles presented Employee Service Awards to Ruben Flores, Karlo Gorgin, Sarah Kiani, Dena Lindamood, Kathy Parks, Dina \u0013 SEQ CHAPTER \\h \\r 1\u0015Shikhpour, and Tony Yin for five years of service, Deborah Steller for ten years of service and Jan Silver for fifteen years of service. Mayor Washburn presented a proclamation to Alan Meyer in recognition of his Los Angeles Lakers� Teacher of the Month Award. Mayor Washburn introduced Dr. Randal Orten, Las Virgenes Municipal Water District, who presented a report regarding the Malibu Creek Runoff Control (MCRC) program. Mayor pro Tem Bozajian spoke regarding the upcoming City election on March 6, 2007.\r\rORAL COMMUNICATIONS - PUBLIC COMMENT\r\r Steve Harris, Mountains Restoration Trust, announced two upcoming events that will be presented by the Mountains Restoration Trust.\r\rCONSENT ITEMS\r\r Approval of the minutes for the January 17, 2007 City Council meeting. \r\r Recommendation to approve a professional services agreement with EdgeSoft, Inc.�in the amount of $883,434.00�for a city-wide permit tracking system.\r\r Recommendation from the Parks, Recreation and Education Commission to award Community Service Grants for the second funding cycle of FY 06/07 as identified in the staff report.\r\r Adoption of Resolution No. 2007-1062, proclaiming March 10, 2007 as �Arbor Day� in the City of Calabasas.\r \r Recommendation from staff and the Civic Center Task Force to amend the professional services agreement for construction management services for the Civic Center with Jones & Jones in the amount of $428,547.00.\r\r Recommendation to approve the filing of the Application, Articles of Incorporation and Bylaws for the Friends of the Arts in Calabasas with the Internal Revenue Service.\r\r Recommendation to approve the appointment of Councilmember Maurer to the California Contract Cities Association Legislative Committee.\r\r Adoption of Resolution No. 2007-1066, executing the Administering-Agency-Federal Master Agreement No. 07-5463R and Program Supplement Agreement No. 012-N to fund the design and repair of Mulholland Highway at post mile marker 27.42 through post mile marker 27.53.\r\rCouncilmember Wolfson \u0013 SEQ CHAPTER \\h \\r 1\u0015moved, seconded by Councilmember Maurer, to approve Consent Items #1, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7 and 8 with the Continuance of Item #2. MOTION CARRIED 5/0. \r\rUNFINISHED BUSINESS\r\r Motion to waive further reading and introduction of Ordinance No. 2007-233, adding Chapter 8.18 to the Calabasas Municipal Code regarding environmentally acceptable food packaging.\r\rAlex Farassati, Environmental Services Manager, presented the staff report.\r\rSamantha Martinez, American Chemistry Council, and Jennifer Forkish, California Grocers Association, spoke in opposition to the proposed ordinance. Ronit Levy, Calabasas, and Michael Friedman, Calabasas, spoke in support of the ordinance and addressed specific language changes in the proposed ordinance. \r\rMayor pro Tem Bozajian moved, seconded by Councilmember Wolfson, to waive further reading and introduce Ordinance No. 2007-233, adding Chapter 8.18 to the Calabasas Municipal Code regarding environmentally acceptable food packaging with revisions. MOTION CARRIED 5/0.\r\rNEW BUSINESS\r\r Update on Mulholland Highway construction � capital improvement projects.\rRobert Yalda, Public Works Director/City Engineer, presented the staff report.\r\rPeter Valk, Chair of Traffic and Transportation Commission, spoke in support of the proposed project.\r\rNo action taken.\r\r \u0013 SEQ CHAPTER \\h \\r 1\u0015Adoption of Resolution No. 2007-1063, approving the acquisition of one Los Angeles County tax-defaulted property in the Calabasas Highlands in the approximate amount of $29,900, plus administration costs (Assessor Parcel Numbers 2072-018-005).\r\rMayor pro Tem Bozajian moved, seconded by Mayor Washburn, to adopt Resolution No. 2007-1063, approving the acquisition of one Los Angeles County tax-defaulted property in the Calabasas Highlands in the approximate amount of $29,900, plus administration costs (Assessor Parcel Numbers 2072-018-005). MOTION CARRIED 5/0.\r\r Adoption of Resolution No. 2007-1064, designating a Preferential Parking District for Park Centre, and for portions of Park Sorrento and Calabasas Road.\r\rThis Item was Continued.\r\r Adoption of Resolution No. 2007-1065, designating a Preferential Parking District on Brandywine Drive.\r\rCouncilmember Wolfson moved, seconded by Councilmember Maurer, to adopt Resolution No. 2007-1065, designating a Preferential Parking District on Brandywine Drive. MOTION CARRIED 5/0.\r\rINFORMATIONAL REPORTS\r\r Check Register for the period of January 5, 2007 to January 25, 2007.\r\rNo action taken.\r\rTASK FORCE REPORTS\r\r Mayor Washburn and Councilmember Maurer spoke regarding upcoming events at Headwaters Corner.\r\rCITY MANAGER�S REPORT \r\r The City Manager indicated that he had nothing to report.\r\rFUTURE AGENDA ITEMS \r\r The City Council requested the following items on future agendas:\r\rInformational issue regarding potential increase in cost of Los Angeles County Sheriff�s services; and\rDiscussion regarding a potential ordinance on adults allowing adolescents to drink alcohol; and\rDiscussion regarding the United States Postal Service moving the Calabasas Post Office to a different location in the City.\r\rADJOURN\r\r The City Council adjourned at 10:26 p.m.\r\r______________________________\rGwen Peirce, CMC\rAssistant City Clerk\r\u0003\r\r\u0004\r\r\u0003\r\r\u0004\r\r\r\r\r\r\u0013PAGE \u0014- 2 -\u0015\r02/07/07\r\r\u0013PAGE \u0014- 2 -\u0015\r02/07/07\r\r\r\r\r\r\u0000\u00